<section>
  <h2>Connecting basketball and data</h2>
  <p>Watching basketball raises questions that highlights alone cannot answer. How should workload be measured? Does a missed game actually indicate an injury? Working on an NBA study helped me see why defining a variable carefully matters as much as plotting it.</p>
  <p>The project used <i>True Shooting Percentage</i> as one measure of efficiency. A crucial lesson was to distinguish an observed association from a causal explanation.</p>
</section>
